---
import { Keycap } from '../../components/Keycap';
import DevPage from '../../layouts/DevPage.astro';
import { cx, SECTION_HEADING } from '../../lib/recipes';
import { THEMES } from '../../lib/themes';
import { PanelOpens } from './_tidy-lab/PanelOpens';
import { Rhythm } from './_tidy-lab/Rhythm';

/*
 * The tidy lab (docs/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md, "Tuning labs"): three of the full tidy's calls that Sean
 * asked to see rather than read (2026-10-18; the eighty-sixth pass in
 * docs/research/findings-0-first-pass.md), side by side with simple state of their own: how a
 * side panel opens beside the box on a wide screen, three ways (PanelOpens); the About page's
 * vertical rhythm with every gap named and measured, a one-step proposal beside it (Rhythm); and
 * the formulas' exact and measured tags with today's pill against the shape token's corner, in
 * every theme. It retires by CLAUDE.md's "Retire a lab" recipe as the calls are decided.
 */

/** The tags as Formulas.astro draws them today (TAG there), and on the shape token's smallest corner. */
const TAG_TODAY = 'rounded-full px-2 text-xs font-medium';
const TAG_PROPOSED = 'rounded-sm px-2 text-xs font-medium';
const EXACT = 'bg-accent-soft text-ink';
const MEASURED = 'bg-surface-raised text-ink-muted';
const LINE = 'mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1 text-sm';
---

<DevPage
  title="tidy lab"
  description="The tidy’s three calls to see: how a side panel opens, About’s section gaps, the tags’ corner."
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    Tidy lab. Three of the tidy’s calls, to see rather than read: how a side panel opens beside the
    box on a wide screen, three ways, each with its own Units tool; the About page’s vertical rhythm
    with every gap named and measured, a one-step proposal beside it; and the formulas’ tags,
    today’s pill against the shape token’s corner, in every theme.
  </Fragment>

  <section class="mt-10" aria-labelledby="opens">
    <h2 id="opens" class={SECTION_HEADING}>
      1. How a side panel opens
    </h2>
    <PanelOpens client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16" aria-labelledby="rhythm">
    <h2 id="rhythm" class={SECTION_HEADING}>
      2. About’s vertical rhythm
    </h2>
    <Rhythm client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16" aria-labelledby="tags">
    <h2 id="tags" class={SECTION_HEADING}>
      3. The formulas’ tags’ corner
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-sm text-ink-muted">
      Every formula’s row ends in a tag, exact or measured. Today the tag is a pill,{' '}
      <code class="font-numeric">rounded-full</code>, a corner from outside the shape tokens, so it
      stays round in every theme, Hardhat’s square corners included. The proposal draws it on{' '}
      <code class="font-numeric">rounded-sm</code>, the keycap’s corner, which each theme sets; a
      keycap sits beside it for the eye.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {THEMES.map((theme) => (
        <section
          data-theme={theme.id}
          aria-labelledby={`tags-${theme.id}`}
          class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-canvas p-5 text-ink"
        >
          <h3 id={`tags-${theme.id}`} class="text-sm font-medium">
            {theme.name}
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-ink-muted">Today, rounded-full</p>
          <p class={LINE}>
            <span class="font-numeric">1 mi = 1,609.344 m</span>
            <span class={cx(TAG_TODAY, EXACT)}>exact</span>
            <span class={cx(TAG_TODAY, MEASURED)}>measured</span>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-ink-muted">Proposed, rounded-sm, the keycap’s corner</p>
          <p class={LINE}>
            <span class="font-numeric">1 lb = 0.45359237 kg</span>
            <span class={cx(TAG_PROPOSED, EXACT)}>exact</span>
            <span class={cx(TAG_PROPOSED, MEASURED)}>measured</span>
            <Keycap label="Esc" />
          </p>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-6 text-sm font-medium">What “extending the guard” means</h3>
    <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose text-sm text-ink-muted">
      The token guard is a lint rule (<code class="font-numeric">eslint.config.js</code>,{' '}
      <code class="font-numeric">RAW_VALUES</code>) that fails{' '}
      <code class="font-numeric">pnpm lint</code> on a class from outside the tokens: a raw color, a
      palette color, a literal duration, and radii such as{' '}
      <code class="font-numeric">rounded-xl</code>. Its radius pattern names xs, xl, 2xl, 3xl, and
      4xl and not <code class="font-numeric">full</code>, so today’s pill passes it. Extending the
      guard adds <code class="font-numeric">full</code> to that pattern: a pill would then fail lint
      like any other untokened corner and could not come back unnoticed. The other way keeps the
      pill as a documented constant, a shape on purpose, and the guard as it is.
    </p>
  </section>
</DevPage>
